    "publish_tier": "daily",
    "importance": "major",
    "summary": "Added MAI-Voice-2.1 and MAI-Voice-2.1 Flash for text-to-speech, with 97 voices per model, MP3 and 24 kHz PCM output, and Quest Pollen access; neither model has an alias. Azure is the primary route, with a Vercel fallback that ultimately also uses Azure and preserves the caller price. The caller price uses a 0.75 multiplier and is billed per UTF-16 character; Gateway cost receipts are preserved. OpenRouter was not added as a route because its TTS billing records could not be reconciled. Validation covered both public speech endpoints, streaming and non-streaming Chat and Responses requests, 10,000-character inputs, bursts, Quest-only access, disconnect/rejoin, one debit per event, and free cache retrieval.",
    "keywords": [
      "MAI-Voice",
      "text-to-speech",
      "Azure",
      "Vercel",
      "audio",
      "Quest Pollen"
    ]
  },
